{
  "id": "80596",
  "type": "Page",
  "tags": [],
  "title": "Amphiprotic Species",
  "content": {
    "bibrefs": [],
    "model": [
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Like water, many molecules and ions may either gain or lose a proton under the appropriate conditions. Such species are said to be "
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "amphiprotic"
                  }
                ],
                "content": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "Describes species that may either donate or accept a proton."
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "3807544462",
                    "type": "p"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "164838606",
                "trigger": "hover",
                "type": "popup"
              },
              {
                "text": ". Another term used to describe such species is "
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "amphoteric"
                  }
                ],
                "content": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "Describes species that can act as either an acid or a base."
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "91682043",
                    "type": "p"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "2552321061",
                "trigger": "hover",
                "type": "popup"
              },
              {
                "text": ", which is a more general term for a species that may act either as an acid or a base by any definition (not just the Brønsted-Lowry one). Consider, for example, the bicarbonate ion, which may either donate or accept a proton, as shown here:"
              }
            ],
            "id": "ypalxcbm9lfnx7a",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "hq8dk9zqrnyv28z",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "d7radbvjxpkrir3",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "\\underset{\\mathrm{acid}}{{\\mathrm{HCO}}_3^-(aq)}\\;+\\;\\underset{\\mathrm{base}}{{\\mathrm H}_2\\mathrm O(l)}\\;\\;\\rightleftharpoons\\;\\;{\\mathrm{CO}}_3^{2-}(aq)\\;+\\;{\\mathrm H}_3\\mathrm O^+(aq)",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "e10oop8rqseisnb",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "4z4bfo9rgvdwhjy",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "\\underset{\\mathrm{base}}{{\\mathrm{HCO}}_3^-(aq)}\\;+\\;\\underset{\\mathrm{acid}}{{\\mathrm H}_2\\mathrm O(l)}\\;\\;\\rightleftharpoons\\;{\\mathrm H}_2{\\mathrm{CO}}_3(aq)\\;+\\;\\mathrm{OH}^-(aq)",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": ""
              }
            ],
            "id": "295779159",
            "type": "p"
          }
        ],
        "id": "411883186",
        "selection": {
          "anchor": {
            "offset": 0,
            "path": [
              0,
              0
            ]
          },
          "focus": {
            "offset": 0,
            "path": [
              1,
              0
            ]
          }
        },
        "type": "content"
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "The hydrogen sulfite (or bisulfite) ion, HSO"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "3"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "−"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", is amphiprotic. Write separate equations representing the reaction of HSO"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "3"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "−"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ":"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "33qydmoc0f6co6l",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "strong": true,
                    "text": "(a)"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " as an acid with OH"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "−"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "gvgepdpwebk3h14",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "strong": true,
                    "text": "(b)"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " as a base with HI"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "ueb95g2yq3no7kv",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "strong": true,
                    "text": "Solution"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "3hek0rpl3iy514g",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "strong": true,
                    "text": "(a)"
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": ""
                      }
                    ],
                    "legacyBlockRendered": true,
                    "src": "{\\mathrm{HSO}}_3^-(aq)\\;+\\;\\mathrm{OH}^-(aq)\\;\\;\\rightleftharpoons\\;\\;{\\mathrm{SO}}_3^{2-}(aq)\\;+\\;{\\mathrm H}_2\\mathrm O(l)",
                    "subtype": "latex",
                    "type": "formula_inline"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ""
                  }
                ],
                "id": "tq2h3r6xb7aws9e",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "strong": true,
                    "text": "(b)"
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": ""
                      }
                    ],
                    "legacyBlockRendered": true,
                    "src": "{\\mathrm{HSO}}_3^-(aq)\\;+\\;\\mathrm{HI}(aq)\\;\\;\\rightleftharpoons\\;\\;{\\mathrm H}_2{\\mathrm{SO}}_3(aq)\\;+\\;\\mathrm I^-(aq)",
                    "subtype": "latex",
                    "type": "formula_inline"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ""
                  }
                ],
                "id": "5jofvkp6gdenrxk",
                "type": "p"
              }
            ],
